<body>
<main class="wrap">
<header class="hero">
<div class="eyebrow">Python · Google Colab</div>
<h1>Get started with Gemini</h1>
<p>Install the Google GenAI SDK, connect a Gemini API key stored in Colab Secrets, and send your first prompts. Run the cells from top to bottom.</p>
<span class="badge">Beginner quick start</span>
</header>
<section class="steps" aria-label="Setup steps">
<article class="card">
<div class="cardhead"><span class="num">1</span><div><h2>Install the packages</h2><p>In a Colab code cell, run this command. The <code class="inline">!</code> tells Colab to run a shell command.</p></div></div>
<div class="codebox"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button><pre><code>!pip install -q "google-genai&gt;=2.12.1,&lt;3" "google-auth==2.49.0"</code></pre></div>
</article>
<article class="card">
<div class="cardhead"><span class="num">2</span><div><h2>Check the installation</h2><p>Run this in a new Python cell to print the installed package versions.</p></div></div>
<div class="codebox"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button><pre><code>from importlib.metadata import version

print("Google GenAI SDK version:", version("google-genai"))
print("Google Auth version:", version("google-auth"))
print("Installation successful!")</code></pre></div>
</article>
<article class="card">
<div class="cardhead"><span class="num">3</span><div><h2>Save your API key in Colab</h2><p>In Colab, open the <strong>Secrets</strong> panel (key icon), add a secret named <code class="inline">GEMINI_API_KEY</code>, paste your key as its value, and allow this notebook to access it.</p></div></div>
<div class="note"><strong>Keep your key private.</strong> Store it in Colab Secrets; don’t paste it directly into a notebook you may share.</div>
</article>
<article class="card">
<div class="cardhead"><span class="num">4</span><div><h2>Connect and send a first prompt</h2><p>This cell reads the saved secret, creates a client, and asks Gemini for a simple explanation.</p></div></div>
<div class="codebox"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button><pre><code>from google import genai
from google.colab import userdata

api_key = userdata.get("GEMINI_API_KEY")
if not api_key:
    raise ValueError("Add GEMINI_API_KEY in the Colab Secrets panel.")

client = genai.Client(api_key=api_key)

response = client.models.generate_content(
    model="gemini-3.5-flash-lite",
    contents="Explain Agentic AI in simple English."
)

print(response.text)</code></pre></div>
<div class="note success">If the response prints, the SDK and API connection are working.</div>
</article>
<article class="card">
<div class="cardhead"><span class="num">5</span><div><h2>Ask for three examples</h2><p>Change the prompt to request a little more detail.</p></div></div>
<div class="codebox"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button><pre><code>response = client.models.generate_content(
    model="gemini-3.5-flash-lite",
    contents="Explain Agentic AI in simple English with 3 examples."
)

print(response.text)</code></pre></div>
</article>
<article class="card">
<div class="cardhead"><span class="num">6</span><div><h2>Ask your own question</h2><p>Enter a question when the cell runs, then print Gemini’s answer.</p></div></div>
<div class="codebox"><button class="copy" type="button">Copy</button><pre><code>question = input("Ask Gemini anything: ")

response = client.models.generate_content(
    model="gemini-3.5-flash-lite",
    contents=question
)

print("Gemini says:")
print(response.text)</code></pre></div>
</article>
</section>
<p class="foot">A Colab notebook quick start · Run setup cells before the prompt examples.</p>
</main>
